{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791316785,"nonce":"MV9oIBfZqicvXCe3ogAcR/zCrQg=","title":"Package sibling types lose to ambient names and enums reuse foreign symbols","message":"At 4aa138bd5de8755550c6bc0a689e0ba6fb830eae, compiling Issue2640 with RAYZOR_E0100_DEBUG=1 shows BytesBuffer, Input and Output resolving Error.OutsideBounds, Error.Blocked and Error.Overflow to the Class symbol from haxe.macro.Expr's Error rather than the haxe.io.Error enum. The resulting imported-module lowering errors install trap stubs. The enum works in an entry module that explicitly imports haxe.io.Error; a plain BytesBuffer probe also works without the macro name collision.\n\nresolve_symbol_in_scope_hierarchy prefers an own-module declaration over an ambient root type, but it does not prefer types declared in sibling modules of the current package. The shared root slot contains whichever namesake was installed last.\n\nEnum pre-registration and lowering also unconditionally reuse the root symbol by simple name. A same.Error enum can therefore turn foreign.Error's Class symbol into an Enum even though the declarations are in different packages.\n\nReproducer: /tmp/rayzor-package-siblings, copied to haxe-conformance/regressions/projects/package_siblings. Native Haxe --interp passes. Before the fix Rayzor fails with an ambiguous value field access and an Enum receiver for new foreign.Error(). The project checks a class and same-name enum in different packages, a sibling's bare enum access, an explicit foreign import, and a local binding shadowing the type name.\n\nRelated but separate: 6ba02daea12113dedb7cc8cfd4c3a69632f8d82a6701b2df7c9db3b96f3c7685 concerns an own-module Error declaration (Issue9533 already passes at this baseline). 0b91874ec5530637ee5c51c6adb960f5ea8354439ad1c845770d9d7ff1d3cd96 tracks class/typedef sharing; this enum work does not establish that broader scope fixed.\n\nBaseline full tiered conformance is 868/1094, 146 skipped, at /tmp/rayzor-dynamic-arithmetic-final-v12/report.tsv. Baseline diagnostics: /tmp/rayzor-io-enum-e0100-issue2640-v12.log and /tmp/rayzor-package-siblings-baseline.log.","files":null}]}